A **translation** adds to the coordinates: right $+x$, left $-x$, up $+y$, down $-y$.

[tikz]\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large},scale=0.6]
\draw[gray!30,very thin](-5,-5)grid(5,5);
\draw[<->](-5.5,0)--(5.5,0)node[right]{$x$};
\draw[<->](0,-5.5)--(0,5.5)node[above]{$y$};
\draw[dashed,->](-3,-2)--(1.9,-2);
\draw[dashed,->](2,-2)--(2,1.9);
\fill(-3,-2)circle(3pt)node[below left]{$P$};
\fill(2,2)circle(3pt)node[above right]{$P'$};
\node[below] at (-0.5,-2.15) {right};
\node[right] at (2.2,1) {up};
\end{tikzpicture}[/tikz]

Reflecting in the **$x$-axis** keeps $x$ the same and changes the **sign of $y$**: $(x, y) \to (x, -y)$.

[tikz]\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large},scale=0.62]
\draw[gray!30,very thin](-4,-4)grid(4,4);
\draw[<->](-4.6,0)--(4.6,0)node[right]{$x$};
\draw[<->](0,-4.6)--(0,4.6)node[above]{$y$};
\draw[dashed](-2.5,2)--(-2.5,-2);
\fill(-2.5,2)circle(3pt)node[above left]{$P$};
\fill(-2.5,-2)circle(3pt)node[below left]{$P'$};
\node[below right,font=\small] at (0.3,-0.1) {mirror line};
\end{tikzpicture}[/tikz]

Reflecting in the **$y$-axis** keeps $y$ the same and changes the **sign of $x$**: $(x, y) \to (-x, y)$.

[tikz]\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large},scale=0.62]
\draw[gray!30,very thin](-4,-4)grid(4,4);
\draw[<->](-4.6,0)--(4.6,0)node[right]{$x$};
\draw[<->](0,-4.6)--(0,4.6)node[above]{$y$};
\draw[dashed](-2.5,2.5)--(2.5,2.5);
\fill(-2.5,2.5)circle(3pt)node[above left]{$P$};
\fill(2.5,2.5)circle(3pt)node[above right]{$P'$};
\node[right,font=\small] at (0.25,-2.2) {mirror line};
\end{tikzpicture}[/tikz]
